<title>CANADA: MacMillan Bloedel Q4 shr turns to loss.</title>
<headline>MacMillan Bloedel Q4 shr turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996		     1995</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$0.60   profit	C$0.50</p>
<p> Net	   loss	72,000   profit	68,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,226,000		1,196,000</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	 profit	C$0.36   profit	C$2.08</p>
<p> Net	 profit	51,000   profit     280,000</p>
<p> Revs		   5,043,000		5,254,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: MacMillan Bloedel Q4 results included C$66 million in restructuring costs and asset writedowns.</p>
<p>Of this amount, C$45 million related to the writedowns of old boilers, which are being replaced at the Powell River paper mill in 1997 and MacMillan's investment in a cement fibre operation in Oregon (American Cemwood).</p>
<p>The remaining C$21 million was for restructuring costs related to streamlining the corporate head office and the business units.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
